(:doc :symbol "asl/agentLoop/exec.asl#" :text "Leon's op dispatch and receipt text, ported from scripts/agentLoop/loop.py (parity: asl/agentLoop/tests/execParityTest.asl against asl/agentLoop/tests/genExecFixture.py): execOp! (execute_op: intent, the effects registry, gate, run as a declared gate, hidden and harness paths, run read hints, run, delete, manage, note, the write and edit prechecks, txn, flush after persisted writes, git ops, done, tree with harness entries hidden, the asl ops, evidence, findings, escalate, raw and recorded), execGateOp!, intentReceipt, execNoteOp, hideHarnessEntries, hiddenTouched, harnessTouched and opWords; formatOpReceipt, formatGateRun, gateTail and gateOutcome (format_op_receipt and its gate helpers); opShapes (_OP_SHAPES), acceptedOpsForMode (get_accepted_ops_for_mode), terminalForms and undeclaredAnswer; collectProseStrings (_collect_prose_strings). The sub-executors are the ported modules: aslOps (asl ops over an injected run), txn, gitOps (git ops and gate runs), runOps (run, delete, manage over the Procs table this module threads). A receipt is the ordered field list of the Python dict (Receipt of Val). Globals the Python read (_receipt_id, _snapshot_before_write, the _WRITTEN journal, _READ_CAP, _RUN_TIMEOUT, _RUN_DEADLINE, _SESSION_ENV, ASL_EVAL_HIDDEN_VARS and the hidden variables' values) are ExecEnv fields and hook functions. Known divergences: an int :argv or :cmd is taken as its digits where the Python raised TypeError; a receipt missing a field format_op_receipt indexes (lines, totalChars, cmd) formats that field as None where the Python raised KeyError; a note answer the core could not produce is a rejected ERR_CORE_HOST_MALFORMED receipt where the Python raised; regex \\s and \\w are ASCII (any byte from 0x80 is a word byte), as in the core.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/agentLoop/exec.asl#rawRequiredBytes" :text "loop.py RAW_REQUIRED_BYTES")
(:doc :symbol "asl/agentLoop/exec.asl#noteMaxChars" :text "loop.py NOTE_MAX_CHARS, about 600 to 800 tokens")
