(:doc :symbol "asl/agentLoop/reply.asl#" :text "Leon's reply parsing, ported from scripts/agentLoop/loop.py (parity: asl/agentLoop/tests/replyParityTest.asl against tests/parity/agentLoop/replyParityGen.py): commit message checks, inner-quote and per-chunk delimiter repair with its locality check (autoRepairReply), cut and degenerate-repeat detection, the reply byte cap, replyFacts over the core, run-as-read, and :raw fence binding. Strings are bytes here: every offset and span is a byte offset (the test maps them to Python's code-point offsets), scans are byte-wise, which equals Python's because every delimiter is ASCII. Known divergence, as in core.asl: Python's Unicode whitespace, letters and digits are ASCII here plus \\x1c-\\x1f as space, and any byte from 0x80 counts as a letter; repr covers ASCII controls and U+0080-U+00A0, U+00AD. The Python core-host error branches (malformed, exit, timeout of the host process) have no counterpart: the core runs in-process.")
